The exported `MeteoriteCatalog` must copy and validate its constructor input. IDs must be positive integers and unique; labels must be non-empty; mass must be finite and nonnegative; notes must be either a string or `null`. Invalid records throw `RangeError` without retaining partial state. `getByLabel` uses exact, case-sensitive matching. `getById` returns the matching record or `null`, including for an empty catalog. `getAll` preserves constructor order. Every returned record must be a fresh copy so callers cannot mutate catalog state.

